{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-71809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is a type I region in two-dimensional space?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-71809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type I region has the property that a vertical line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type I region is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/d74059ee4370e106b54917ec43b007327805049033752867473d08da850001bf.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-71809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8520f561996cbff88d81d09e9e399101a6c1536c5dacc3d385980dab31a0d4b0"} {"question" "q-71809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-71809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/3edfe230c7156c19aedb2abe318717048bc22fba9475dadccc41047fcc0a6b53.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/82ed2a77b4017b904ea94ed11e7febb76385bc64082acee5ad3c2e1304fae22c.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/847a7a418ef19d023ba16122c7c0da3cf400a5467001c51ee0315b5c978a17db.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/8e3cc81bc5269e4ae85516f2173e1d61b47a1c887f9e1532f914226333e09184.png"] ["text" "None of the listed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-71809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/3edfe230c7156c19aedb2abe318717048bc22fba9475dadccc41047fcc0a6b53.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-71816" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/438b119b6fd2c2f066705f9f44053faa766e3f57b6ee1a614794febf7a517a12.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type I region in two-dimensional space?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-71816" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type I region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $x:$\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{y-3}\\,⟹\\,y={x}^{2}+3\n$$\n\nThe function $y=1$ is already written as a function of $x.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the vertical lines $x=0$ and $x=1.$ So, we have $0\\le x\\le 1.$\n\nWe draw a vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower function $g(x)$ and the upper function $f(x).$ A vertical line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type I region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/43b35101f6c57352975f3667ca76dece5782326c9af008990c8820a71bed504d.png)\n\nThe vertical line enters the region through the lower function $y=1$ and leaves through the upper function $y={x}^{2}+3.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+3.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-71816" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8520f561996cbff88d81d09e9e399101a6c1536c5dacc3d385980dab31a0d4b0"} {"que