home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-72055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/7231c566a92c547b6fa950052ddfbe90cf08faf794937295226c468764701a3d.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-73552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the ellipses $(x-1)^{2}+4{y}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=4?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-73552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/215dd0c920e700a75896fc54751ec20d197487a2c992cd8910810c66129c14dc.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/7e1a0c5dd2b4aadf7efe78d903234b8d00cf4fa92eb7a3b41209a856f2d14b01.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=0.25$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/a90d7306e3f88a31609e368f9362248d6a12b7922b6a9e8c9f980ab31e7fb140.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-73552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8520f561996cbff88d81d09e9e399101a6c1536c5dacc3d385980dab31a0d4b0"} {"question" "q-73552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-73552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-73552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-72185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region inside the circumference ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-72185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,x=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,y=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/0960063edcce8ccd55dc2f77147c4a4982645c180e8b998d7e520c65131ea045.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-72185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8520f561996cbff88d81d09e9e399101a6c1536c5dacc3d385980dab31a0d4b0"} {"question" "q-72185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-72185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-72185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-168921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ and the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=1?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-168921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/bc6b71d1fe69abd34dbd939dc62ede5201b75713e25456cf084e889bc44f449e.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.4$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/4a1fd7069abaa3b3fa4d9c286773d226798bf3ad565e85663cab44557fd635c1.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=-1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/260e8e959ca95a029a98bd4102106a66df418ea73c0640398c8fdebfdbf812f6.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-168921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8520f561996cbff88d81d09e9e399101a6c1536c5dacc3d385980dab31a0d4b0"} {"question" "q-168921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3e85eeaf498d17c8a2f26f32fa9b331cf5d99d6c1dbe851af50132414a39f8b"} {"question" "q-168921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] 